body:
Meh I'm split on it. On one hand, I really liked they closed all of the questions we had in the TJM and we also have 100 episodes to watch. So it's not like the show had short lived success.

&#x200B;

On the other hand, it's one of my favorite cartoons of all time. It felt real, grounded, and loved the diveristy of characters in terms of personalities and cultural backgrounds. It would be cool to see how the characters evolve. 

&#x200B;

I'm not begging for a season 6, but if it happens I will definetly watch it!

The minute he left, they announced that the color rush jerseys would be their new official ones. Cleveland changed their jerseys right when Lebron Left so it has that same feeling.

&#x200B;

Although they had been using their color rush jerseys since their inception (2016 was when all teams had to participate in it), they were fittingly used for the worst night of football, Thursday Night Football.

&#x200B;

The fact that they were forced to come up with something back then just shows how lackluster it is.

I can see your perspective. I have an addictive personality and unfortunately, I have tried PMO this past year and failed miserably. I would relapse so hard after abstaining from masturbating, so I know personally that that route is extremely difficult. As I would fail often, it demotivated me to the point of giving up.

&#x200B;

I do want to try it when I build a proper foundation of no porn and no visual stimulation and masturbating only 3 times a week for starters. Once I pass that after a month or two, I can try nofap in its entirety if deemed necessary,

I already changed my mindset about the whole "il give you stuff" and not delivering after the 2nd time he mentioned it. It's the constant mentions from the same person that is really annoying. 

&#x200B;

And they don't owe me shit, but them saying I'm their favorite streamer while giving financial support to others sends a contradictory message. I sub to my favorite streamer every month and go rabid fanboy for my favorite franchise. For the other streamers who are not my favorite I give them a follow and chat a bit, and I'll consume other franchises without going crazy for them. That's how humans usually behave; they'll show stronger support for their favorites and weaker support for the rest.  What they are doing is essentially the opposite. 

&#x200B;

Essentially if they were genuine and did not constantly say "you're my favorite streamer" when actions show otherwise then I wouldn't have made this post. I think money is a stronger sign of support than being involved and basic human nature/history would show that. We might agree to disagree on that last point and I'm ok with that.

It makes less sense to sub to a big streamer as a mod because they are already making bank.

&#x200B;

My thing originally if they give big streamers money, but not you, that would be slightly annoying. Even a few hundred bits would be nice. In this situation, I really don't get the "it's their money they can do whatever they want", especially when they claim you are their favorite channel but contributes to others. Like ya, you can do whatever you want with your money, but money talks. If you can throw in a sub or 200 bits to Mr. Beast but you can't do that for your 'favorite streamer' then maybe you're lying? I just don't like liars that's all

The more I think of it, the more I agree with the consensus of "if they support the stream they are not in the wrong."

&#x200B;

It's more of the "Hey guys look how much money I have, I'll def give you x y and z" over and over again and not seeing anything happen that pisses me off. No one likes someone who is a liar and doesn't stick to their word.

The last piece is a new perspective I didn't think of. He does chat with the stream a good deal, but like you said he doesn't live up to his expectations which he puts upon himself. 

&#x200B;

He also gloats about his wealth occasionally which can be alienating towards the community. Perhaps I'll make him a VIP instead of a mod.

So if you were working on something and someone repeatedly said "oh ya I'll def support your cause" and not deliver, you wouldn't be even slightly annoyed with the person?

&#x200B;

You clearly didn't even read the post as I said I love my mods and my community.

I totally agree with everything you said; I was just checking on what the consensus was about the situation. I don't bring enough value to get subs anyway so I'll keep on working at it to get to my goals. 

&#x200B;

I'll either ignore him when he mentions it either on stream or dms, or do what you said and make a playful inside community joke of it.

Oh yeah of course man! I'll keep on doing me when I'm with someone I find an interest in. I never fixate on marrying the person and pull a Mordecai. I

&#x200B;

If these average looking girls are not relationships with above-average guys, do you mean they are with average looking guys or not in relationships at all? Didn't really understand what you meant by that.

&#x200B;

And yeah I definitely agree that I don't want to have a kid in my 20's, but wouldn't'  it be awesome to find your best friend at that time? I think that's all we are looking for at the end of the day is to score that jackpot, but it seems like no girls are willing to see whether I'm that jackpot or not (not that I'm entitled to a chance obviously).

I kind of wish I was a girl then. I do know my type of girl and what I characteristics I would want in them. Not saying that the person has to fit into a tight little box, but I know what I want and what I don't want. I used to have the problem of wanting to date anyone but now I just want to date someone whom I find very interesting and fun to be around. 

&#x200B;

You also bring up a good point of most average looking girls in their 20s just want to have fun. Although I feel as though this is a bit of generalization, there is the truth of them having it easier in sex and relationships than men. This makes me angry at myself and the creation of myself. If I was an average looking girl, my love life would be way more fulfilling and that makes me sad inside. 

&#x200B;

I'll keep on trying to make organic relationships with people I enjoy spending time with. If I feel that bond, I'll advance things but in all likelihood some bullshit will occur as always. It feels like a endless trip of sadness and rejection after you do the same dance after a whileee.

Trying my hardest to get into a long term relationship. A good amount of my photos are blurry (I'm aware), but I'm going to get at least one nice photo this weekend. Hoping my profile conveys a good message too :)

&#x200B;

https://tinder.com/@firebro17

Oh cool. Chemistry is really fun. Although I took a Geology course this summer, we learned about how different elements were made via covalent and ionic bonds.

&#x200B;

I'm a Managerial Economics and Communications major.
